const faqItems = [
  {
    question: 'What is the divorce rate in the UAE?',
    answer: 'Official UAE divorce figures are published emirate by emirate, and they measure different things, so there is no single headline rate to quote. The most recent official numbers: Dubai Courts registered 2,285 divorce cases in 2024, and the divorce rate for Emirati couples in Dubai was 1.96 per 1,000 Emiratis of marriage age (Dubai Statistics Center). Ministry of Justice data put 2024 divorces at the federal courts of Sharjah, Ajman, Fujairah and Umm Al Quwain at 448 to 473, depending on the report. Ras Al Khaimah courts registered 485 divorces in 2023, and the latest Abu Dhabi yearbook figure we could verify is 2,086 divorces in 2019.',
