  },
  {
    question: 'How does the 2022 civil law change the divorce numbers?',
    answer: 'Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2022 has given non-Muslims a civil, no-fault divorce route in the UAE since 1 February 2023, alongside the Abu Dhabi Civil Family Court under Abu Dhabi Law No. 14 of 2021. Divorces that once went through home-country courts may now appear in UAE court records, so compare pre-2023 and post-2023 counts with care. In Dubai, divorces between two non-Emiratis rose from 1,396 in 2023 to 1,644 in 2024; the official report does not give reasons, and population growth may also play a part.',
